Inquisitor Penitence met the Party at the [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/index|Inquisition]]'s office at two in the morning, after [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] asked for him or for Inquisitor Absolution by name. He is tall, and his raiment is identical to every other Inquisitor's, where raiments are usually a little different for each person. Where [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/People/Brother Zeal|Brother Zeal]] has pearlescent writing on his forehead, Penitence has the same mother-of-pearl material worked into tattoos on his forearms. When he takes notes, his writing flows off of his arm and onto the page. He gives away almost nothing, and his expression is hard to read.

He led the Party into a questioning room below the lobby, at a plain metal table under a single light, and asked them to tell the whole story from the beginning. He took their report seriously. The room held a golden bell that rang whenever a true thing was said. He told them the Inquisition would take the matter of the [[Gas-n-Go Heart|Heart]] and the radar dish from there, and refused to pass anything they had brought him to anyone outside the Inquisition, even Cardinal Weatherhead. He paid them 125 gold as a gesture of goodwill.
